{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) given that the area of rectangle \\(PQRS\\) is 24 and \\(TQ = TR\\). Let's proceed step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   Let the length of the rectangle \\(PQRS\\) be \\(l\\) and the width be \\(w\\). Therefore, the area of the rectangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   l \\times w = 24\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the coordinates of the points:**\n   Place the rectangle in the coordinate plane with \\(P\\) at \\((0, w)\\), \\(Q\\) at \\((l, w)\\), \\(R\\) at \\((l, 0)\\), and \\(S\\) at \\((0, 0)\\). Point \\(T\\) is on the line segment \\(QR\\) such that \\(TQ = TR\\). Since \\(QR\\) is vertical, \\(T\\) must be at the midpoint of \\(QR\\).\n\n3. **Find the coordinates of \\(T\\):**\n   The coordinates of \\(Q\\) are \\((l, w)\\) and the coordinates of \\(R\\) are \\((l, 0)\\). The midpoint \\(T\\) of \\(QR\\) is:\n   \\[\n   T = \\left(l, \\frac{w + 0}{2}\\right) = \\left(l, \\frac{w}{2}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the area of quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\):**\n   The quadrilateral \\(PTRS\\) can be divided into two triangles: \\(\\triangle PTS\\) and \\(\\triangle PRT\\).\n\n","prefix_end":1102,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,3082,315,29136,42939,17767,47605,50,57758,2661,429,279,3082,315,22756,17767,47,90506,57758,374,220,17,19,323,17767,51,48,284,4984,59,568,6771,594,10354,3019,553,3019,382,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,15336,315,279,22756,25,1019,256,6771,279,3084,315,279,22756,17767,47,90506,57758,387,17767,75,57758,323,279,2374,387,17767,86,59,568,15277,11,279,3082,315,279,22756,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,326,1124,15136,289,284,220,17,19,198,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,35,24308,279,13934,315,279,3501,25,1019,256,10771,279,22756,304,279,16184,11031,448,17767